fn generate_github_alternative_url(url: &str) -> Option<(ureq::Agent, String)> {
  if !url.starts_with("https://github.com/") {
    return None;
  }

  generate_github_mirror_url_from_template(url)
    .or_else(|| generate_github_mirror_url_from_base(url))
    .map(|_alt_url| {
      (
        ureq::Agent::config_builder()
          .user_agent(BUNDLER_USER_AGENT)
          .build()
          .into(),
        url.to_owned(),
      )
    })
}

findings.body:
`generate_github_alternative_url` now binds the computed mirror URL to `_alt_url` and returns `url.to_owned()`. The mirror lookup still runs, but its result is never used. Any user who sets `TAURI_BUNDLER_TOOLS_GITHUB_MIRROR` or `TAURI_BUNDLER_TOOLS_GITHUB_MIRROR_TEMPLATE` (documented in `ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES.md`) will still download from github.com. In regions where GitHub is blocked, that means NSIS or WiX downloads fail, and the mirror feature regresses silently.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="50-60"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The only functional change left in this path is the user agent on the mirror agent, and that agent is never used with a mirror URL. Restore the original `alt_url` binding and return it, as in the base code.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="52-59"}
.map(|alt_url| {
  (
    ureq::Agent::config_builder()
      .user_agent(BUNDLER_USER_AGENT)
      .build()
      .into(),
    alt_url,
  )
})

`crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json` changes `"tauri"` from `2.9.2` to `2.9.3`. That field is not tied to the CLI version. It is the version of the `tauri` crate that generated projects depend on: `init.rs` and `plugin/init.rs` format it into `tauri = { version = "<metadata.tauri>" }`. This PR does not bump `crates/tauri/Cargo.toml` (still `2.9.2`), so a project created by this CLI would depend on a `tauri` version that is not published. The `tauri` value looks like it came from a find-and-replace of the CLI version. The `tauri-build` and `tauri-plugin` entries (2.5.1) were correctly left alone.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="1-9"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Revert `"tauri"` to `"2.9.2"` unless the `tauri` crate is also being released in this PR. The `cli.js` version (2.9.3) should stay as is.

The diff drops `#[cfg(target_os = "windows")]` from the `Sha256` enum variant and from its `verify_hash` match arm. This is not part of a version bump or the listed changelog entries. The change compiles, because `sha2` is an unconditional dependency, and `#[allow(dead_code)]` covers the rest. It does mean the SHA-256 path is now compiled on every platform, even though its only caller (WiX, `msi/mod.rs`) is Windows-only. If the removal is intentional, it belongs in its own PR with a changelog entry. Otherwise, restore the gates.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-bundler/src/utils/http_utils.rs" lines="97-102"}

The `verify_hash` match arm at line 120 has the same change.
